Scope
Id	Statement
scope.1	This specification defines void-os, an operating system for language models and agents in which every datum is a relation in normal form held as MTSV text: a data bank that keeps what a harness sends, tools through which a model reads it and any other file, hooks through which a harness reaches both, and a view through which a person sees the whole of it.
scope.2	void-os is six groups, the relational model, the data bank, the tools, the hooks, the view, and system generation, which holds the decisions postponed to release and how void-os is built, described and installed; the relational model writes every datum as a relation and operates on it, the data bank keeps relations, and the tools, the hooks and the view stand on both; the Modules sheet gives each and its secret.
scope.3	The classes of products are the components of the Components sheet whose Product is true.
scope.4	void-os runs on the machine of the person who installs it, for that person alone, and is the same product in each of its two implementations, in Python and in JavaScript.
scope.5	Out of scope: a remote server, accounts, sharing between persons, and any harness's own configuration format, which each harness documents.
