Clause
Id	Statement
clause.1	This specification defines void-os: the components of the Components sheet whose Product is true, each a class of products, labelled by its Component as a conforming void-os, conforming when it meets every requirement of the module whose access program starts it, of every module that access program reaches, and of void-os, the root.
clause.2	The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
clause.3	Every sheet of this specification is normative but Scope, which is informative.
clause.12	This specification's books follow the register rows their References name, and .mapping.mtsv the register rows of the sources of each notation it writes the books in, Python, JavaScript, JSON and TOML; the register reaches void-os through these two only, and nothing generated from them reads it.
clause.15	This specification defines no optional feature and deprecates none; its one extension is a format, added under conversion in the Modules sheet.
clause.26	void-os is carried out twice, in Python and in JavaScript, each implementation a conforming void-os on its own, the two passing the same conformance cases.
clause.27	Every requirement of this specification states one requirement: one thought, one subject and one predicate, and one key word.
